# FeF3, rhombohedral ReO3-type, space group R-3c (#167).
# Source: Crystallography Open Database entry 2100647 ("On the Compression
# Mechanism of FeF3", Acta Crystallographica Section B), hexagonal setting.
# This is the HIGH-PRESSURE phase's cell (smaller than the ambient phase) —
# kept in this project as a deliberately-wrong-but-plausible candidate for
# gsas2_candidate_sweep.py's demo manifest (Data/FeF3/sweep_demo.json),
# alongside the correct ambient-pressure structure
# (fef3_r3c_ambient.cif) — both use the same (correct) Cu wavelength, so
# the sweep isolates "which structure" rather than "which wavelength."
data_FeF3_COD_2100647
_cell_length_a                   4.6866
_cell_length_b                   4.6866
_cell_length_c                   13.3677
_cell_angle_alpha                90.0
_cell_angle_beta                 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma                120.0
_space_group_name_H-M_alt        'R -3 c'
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M   'R -3 c'
_space_group_IT_number           167
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number      167

